{"id": "2026-10-22-news-strike-on-dammam-airport-kills-two", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Strike on Dammam airport kills two", "summary": "A strike on Dammam's King Fahd International Airport on 21 October killed two and injured eight, and the US ordered non-essential staff out of its Riyadh embassy amid Houthi attacks.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-orders-some-diplomats-to-leave-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-threat/a-79727353", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing", "single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "A strike on King Fahd International Airport in Dammam, in eastern Saudi Arabia, on the evening of Wednesday 21 October killed two people and injured eight, Saudi Arabia's civil aviation authority said, and Washington ordered non-essential US embassy staff to leave Riyadh. The authority did not say who carried out the attack, and the Houthis did not claim it; flights from the airport were diverted as operations stopped. Earlier on Wednesday, the Saudi energy ministry said a drone aimed at an oil facility was shot down but its debris killed two workers, a Filipino and a Nepali national, and injured two others. State Department spokesperson Tommy Pigott said the Iran-backed Houthis had \"increasingly engaged in hostilities against Saudi Arabia\", including attacks on civilian airports. Reuters and AFP, citing unnamed sources, reported similar departure orders for other Gulf states; Pigott called those reports \"inaccurate\" and said only staff in Saudi Arabia were affected. A four-year truce between Riyadh and the Houthis broke down during the Iran war, and Saudi Arabia has faced near-daily attacks this month.", "why": "after the 10 October strike on Riyadh's airport, a second major Saudi airport has now been hit, and the US evacuation order shows Washington expects the attacks to continue.", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-strike-on-dammam-airport-kills-two", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Saudi Arabia", "Houthis", "Dammam", "US State Department"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-icc-wins-eu-sakharov-prize", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "ICC wins EU Sakharov Prize", "summary": "The European Parliament awarded the 2026 Sakharov Prize to the International Criminal Court and its officials, citing US sanctions on the court.", "url": "https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/press-room/20261018IPR48263/the-international-criminal-court-and-its-officials-awarded-the-sakharov-prize", "source_domain": "europarl.europa.eu", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The European Parliament on Thursday 22 October awarded its 2026 Sakharov Prize for Freedom of Thought jointly to the International Criminal Court (ICC) and its officials. Announcing the prize in the chamber, Parliament President Roberta Metsola said it recognises \"the Court's important work in upholding international law and justice\". The Hague court tries individuals for genocide, war crimes, crimes against humanity and aggression, as a court of last resort when national courts do not act. Parliament's announcement links the award to the \"various waves of sanctions imposed since 2025 on the ICC, notably by the USA\", on its prosecutors, judges and staff, which MEPs have called serious attacks on international justice. It repeats MEPs' call for the European Commission to activate the EU \"blocking statute\", a law that voids the effect of foreign sanctions inside the EU, to protect ICC officials.", "why": "the EU's main human-rights prize is going to an institution, not a person, and it puts Parliament publicly against US policy on the court.", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-icc-wins-eu-sakharov-prize", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["European Parliament", "International Criminal Court", "Roberta Metsola", "Sakharov Prize"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-russia-strikes-kyiv-after-witkoff-talks", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russia strikes Kyiv after Witkoff talks", "summary": "Russian attacks on Kyiv killed one and injured 22 and Ukraine sent 630 drones at the Moscow region, after Witkoff met Putin; the Kremlin said it was open in principle to talks.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/22/russian-strikes-hit-kyiv-after-witkoff-meets-putin", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Russian attacks on Kyiv overnight into Thursday 22 October killed at least one person and injured 22, including four children, Ukraine's emergency service said, a day after US envoy Steve Witkoff met Vladimir Putin in St Petersburg. Kyiv mayor Vitali Klitschko said metro infrastructure at the Pivdenny Bridge was damaged. Moscow mayor Sergei Sobyanin said Ukraine had launched 630 drones at the Moscow region, 163 of them at the capital, wounding two people; he said most were shot down. The Kremlin said it was willing \"in principle\" to resume US-mediated talks with Ukraine but saw little \"substance\" in Ukrainian and European proposals, while Donald Trump said the war may be as close as it has ever been to ending. RFI reports that Moscow says it is ready for three-way talks with Washington and Kyiv in mid-November. Ukrainian foreign minister Andrii Sybiha wrote that \"appeasement, servility, and flattery will not stop this war\".", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-russia-strikes-kyiv-after-witkoff-talks", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kyiv", "Steve Witkoff", "Kremlin"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-new-mexico-judge-fines-meta-25bn", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "New Mexico judge fines Meta $25bn", "summary": "A New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25 billion for misleading Facebook users about data privacy in the Cambridge Analytica case.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/am%C3%A9riques/20261022-%C3%A9tats-unis-meta-sanctionn%C3%A9-de-25-milliards-de-dollars-pour-avoir-tromp%C3%A9-les-utilisateurs-de-facebook", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "tech"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay the state $25 billion on Wednesday 21 October for misleading Facebook users about the privacy of their data. Judge Francis Mathew wrote that \"Facebook promised users that they (the users) controlled their data. This was false.\" He said state law would justify a penalty of more than $219 billion but reduced it to $25 billion. New Mexico sued in 2021 over the Cambridge Analytica scandal, in which a third-party quiz app harvested data from up to 87 million Facebook profiles for political targeting, and it is the only state to take that case to trial. Meta's chief legal officer said the company expects to win on appeal and called the case an attempt \"to impose a tax on speech\".", "why": "it is one of the largest penalties a single US state has won against a company, and it comes on top of $942 million New Mexico already won from Meta in a separate case over harm to minors, which Meta is also appealing.", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-new-mexico-judge-fines-meta-25bn", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Meta", "New Mexico", "Cambridge Analytica", "Facebook"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-taiz-fighting-pushes-yemen-displacement-to-260-0", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Taiz fighting pushes Yemen displacement to 260,000", "summary": "OCHA says almost 260,000 people have been displaced in Yemen since August as government-Houthi fighting intensifies around Taiz.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/22/fighting-rages-in-yemens-taiz-as-un-warns-nearly-260000-now-displaced", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Almost 260,000 people have been displaced in Yemen since August, the UN humanitarian office OCHA said late on Wednesday 21 October, as fighting between government forces and the Houthis intensifies around the city of Taiz. About half of them have taken refuge in Taiz itself. The UN Human Rights Office has verified 251 civilian casualties, 57 killed and 194 injured; half of those killed were children. A spokesperson for the Saudi-backed government forces claimed 835 operations against the Houthis and 285 Houthi fighters killed or injured; those figures could not be checked. Aid groups have reached about 174,000 displaced people, and families say shelter is their most urgent need.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-taiz-fighting-pushes-yemen-displacement-to-260-0", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Yemen", "Taiz", "Houthis", "OCHA"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-strasbourg-faults-swiss-court-in-keller-case", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Strasbourg faults Swiss court in Keller case", "summary": "The ECHR found Switzerland's Federal Supreme Court breached Brian Keller's fair-hearing right (B.K. v. Switzerland), awarding EUR 5,000 costs, and rejected his detention-conditions complaints.", "url": "https://hudoc.echr.coe.int/eng?i=001-252962", "source_domain": "hudoc.echr.coe.int", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The European Court of Human Rights ruled unanimously on Thursday 22 October that Switzerland breached Brian Keller's right to a fair hearing, while rejecting his complaints about his conditions of detention. In the judgment, published as B.K. v. Switzerland, the Court found that the Federal Supreme Court had obtained information on its own initiative, namely that he had allegedly wrecked a special cell built to give him daily yard access, and relied on it, at least in part, to dismiss his appeal as abusive without letting him comment. His complaint that he was denied outdoor exercise at weekends and on public holidays at Pöschwies prison between July 2019 and October 2020 was declared inadmissible. Switzerland must pay EUR 5,000 for his legal costs; the Court said finding a violation was itself enough redress for any non-pecuniary damage. Several Swiss outlets reported \"5,000 francs in compensation\", but the judgment awards euros, for costs. It becomes final only if neither side asks for a referral to the Grand Chamber within three months.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-strasbourg-faults-swiss-court-in-keller-case", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["European Court of Human Rights", "Brian Keller", "Federal Supreme Court", "Pöschwies"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-swiss-hostage-reported-freed-from-niger", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss hostage reported freed from Niger", "summary": "A Swiss woman and an Austrian woman kidnapped in Niger in 2025 were reported freed and flown to Benghazi, Libya; the FDFA had not confirmed.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/in-libyen-eingetroffen-schweizer-und-oesterreichische-geisel-aus-niger-befreit", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A 69-year-old Swiss woman and an Austrian woman kidnapped in Niger in 2025 have been reported freed and flown to Benghazi in eastern Libya, the Libyan channel al-Masar said overnight into Thursday 22 October. The Swiss woman was abducted in Agadez in April 2025 and the Austrian in January 2025. In a video aired by al-Masar, both thanked Marshal Khalifa Haftar, who controls eastern Libya, and his son Saddam for their release; Reuters judged the photos authentic. As of Thursday morning, Switzerland's foreign ministry (FDFA) had not commented, and Austria's foreign ministry said the release and handover process was not yet complete. It is unclear who held the women and how they were freed.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-swiss-hostage-reported-freed-from-niger", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Niger", "Libya", "Khalifa Haftar", "FDFA"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-bern-rejects-urgent-credit-clawback-bill", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bern rejects urgent-credit clawback bill", "summary": "The Federal Council recommended parliament not take up initiative 24.400, which would give legal effect to parliament's later rejection of urgent credits.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/v6lLyn4lTfzZ", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Council said on Wednesday 21 October that parliament should not take up a National Council committee bill under which parliament's later rejection of an emergency credit would always have legal effect. Under the Finance Act, an urgent federal payment needs prior approval from parliament's Finance Delegation, and the full parliament votes on it afterwards; today a rejection at that stage does not undo what was already committed. The National Council's political institutions committee (initiative 24.400) wants a rejection to force the government to claw back money already spent and unwind contracts. The Federal Council says that would badly limit its ability to act in a crisis and expose the Confederation to financial and legal risk, because partners could no longer rely on its commitments. The best-known case is the 2023 Credit Suisse rescue, when the National Council rejected the emergency guarantees after they had been granted, with no legal effect.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-bern-rejects-urgent-credit-clawback-bill", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "National Council", "Finance Delegation"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-federal-court-upholds-sperisen-sentence", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Federal court upholds Sperisen sentence", "summary": "Switzerland's Federal Supreme Court rejected Erwin Sperisen's appeal, confirming his 14-year sentence for complicity in the 2006 Pavón prison killings.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/erwin-sperisen-n-a-rien-d-un-innocent-aux-yeux-du-tribunal-federal", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Supreme Court has rejected Erwin Sperisen's appeal in full, confirming his 14-year sentence for complicity in the 2006 killing of seven inmates at Guatemala's Pavón prison, Le Temps reported on Thursday 22 October. Sperisen, a Swiss-Guatemalan dual national, headed Guatemala's national civil police at the time. Geneva's court convicted him again on 12 September 2024 at a fourth trial, which was needed after the European Court of Human Rights found that one of the appeal judges had not been impartial. The Federal Supreme Court found no breach of the presumption of innocence and no arbitrary weighing of evidence, and said the defence's procedural battles were partly to blame for the case's length.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-federal-court-upholds-sperisen-sentence", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Erwin Sperisen", "Federal Supreme Court", "Guatemala"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-bvg-survivor-and-disability-pensions-rise-in-202", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "BVG survivor and disability pensions rise in 2027", "summary": "Mandatory occupational survivor and disability pensions will rise with inflation on 1 January 2027, by 2.1% for pensions begun in 2023.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/pW3JVIm6ZZcy", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Mandatory occupational pensions (BVG/LPP) for survivors and people with disabilities will rise with inflation on Friday 1 January 2027, the Federal Council said on Thursday 22 October. Pensions that began in 2023 rise by 2.1% for the first time. Pensions first adjusted on 1 January 2026 rise by 1.0%, and those last adjusted on 1 January 2025 by 1.2%, because AHV/AVS old-age pensions are also being adjusted in 2027. The rule covers only the legal minimum; pensions above it are raised only if each pension fund's board decides it can afford to.", "why": "if you receive one of these pensions, the adjustment applies automatically only to the statutory minimum part, and your fund's annual report says whether it raises the rest.", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-bvg-survivor-and-disability-pensions-rise-in-202", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2027-01-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "BVG", "AHV"]}
{"id": "2026-10-22-news-magnitude-3-5-quake-near-les-diablerets", "date": "2026-10-22", "stream": "news", "headline": "Magnitude 3.5 quake near Les Diablerets", "summary": "A magnitude 3.5 earthquake struck about 7 km south of Les Diablerets (VD) on 22 October; no damage expected.", "url": "http://eida.ethz.ch/fdsnws/event/1/query?starttime=2026-10-22T00:00:00&minmagnitude=2.5&format=text", "source_domain": "eida.ethz.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A magnitude 3.5 earthquake struck about seven kilometres south of Les Diablerets (VD) at 10:45 on Thursday 22 October, the Swiss Seismological Service (SED) at ETH Zurich recorded. The SED catalogue puts its depth at about 5 km. It was likely felt over a wide area, but quakes of this size do not normally cause damage. The SED records 1,000 to 1,500 earthquakes in Switzerland each year, and people feel only 10 to 20 of them.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-22-news-magnitude-3-5-quake-near-les-diablerets", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-22", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Swiss Seismological Service", "Les Diablerets", "Vaud"]}
